% Test file with multiple SRSW violations
% This file should report ALL violations, not just the first one
%
% Each procedure is declared, with the wildcard at each position in the mode
% its head uses it, so the file is a typed program (TGLP Definition "Typed GLP
% Program", condition 1) and is refused by the SRSW pass, which is its subject,
% not by the type checker for an undeclared procedure.

% Violation 1: X appears twice as writer
procedure bad1(_?, _?).
bad1(X, X) :- true.

% Violation 2: Y? appears twice without ground guard
procedure bad2(_, _).
bad2(Y?, Y?) :- true.

% Violation 3: Z has no reader
procedure bad3(_?).
bad3(Z) :- true.

% This one is correct
procedure good(_?, _).
good(A, A?) :- true.
